Description: avfilter/tonemapx: round 10-bit samples on the NEON path
 The NEON routines added TEN_BIT_ROUNDING, 512, before shifting by
 TEN_BIT_SCALE_SHIFT, 19, where rounding needs 2^18. So every 10-bit
 sample they wrote was truncated: half a code low on average, and a
 neutral grey came out with Cb and Cr 511 instead of 512. Their 10-bit
 input conversion added the same 512 before a shift by 9, where the C
 and x86 paths add 256. Linux arm64 and macOS arm64 run this path.
 .
 Round as the C path does: add 2^18 before the output shift and 2^8
 before the input shift. TEN_BIT_ROUNDING has no other use and goes.
 .
 Cross-compiled for aarch64 and run under emulation, the NEON path
 now writes the same bytes as the x86 C path on 10 of 12 outputs of
 plain PQ, HLG and Dolby Vision profile 5 input, and within one code on
 the rest. Before, 10-bit output had 50 % of its samples one code below
 the C path's. 8-bit output keeps its rounding.
